      "source": "minerals/2-uncommon/ores/platinum-ore/index.md",
      "content": "---\ntitle: Platinum Ore\nslug: platinum-ore\ntype: item\nkingdom: Mineral\nitem_class: Uncommon\ncategory: Ore\nsubcategory: Metal\nmaterial_type: Metal\nmaterial_form: Ore\nmaterial_family: Platinum\nsource_items: []\nrefines_into: Platinum Ingot\nrefinement_ratio: \"4:1\"\nweight_class: Medium\ndurability: High\nenchantment_affinity: \"40% (+3 dice)\"\nmarket_value: 8\nmarket_price: null\npricing_status: needs-completion\ntags:\n  - items\n  - minerals\n  - metal\n  - ore\n  - uncommon\nvisibility: public\n---\n\n# Platinum Ore\n\n## Effect\nPlatinum Ore contains highly pure metallic veins that conduct magical energy with exceptional stability, making it one of the most valuable refinement materials for enchantment-focused crafting.\n\n---\n\n## Lore\nKnown as the *“Metal of Divinity,”* platinum is said to form where celestial energy seeps into the earth. Some believe it is the crystallised essence of fallen stars.\n\n---\n\n## Material & Crafting Traits\n- High purity with minimal impurities  \n- Extremely difficult to extract and refine  \n- Resistant to corruption and decay  \n- Found in deep or magically saturated environments  \n\n---\n\n## Refinement\n- Smelts into: [[Platinum Ingot]]\n- Ratio: 4 Ore → 1 Ingot\n- Notes: Requires advanced or stable forge conditions\n\n---\n\n## Alloy Use\n- High-tier alloys (future)\n\n---\n\n## Enchantment Use\n- Strong affinity with Light and Celestial magic  \n- Maintains enchantment stability under heavy use  \n\n---\n\n## Quote\n*\"From the heavens it fell — and to the heavens it answers.\"*\n"
